  autoCollectReward: 0
  featureUnlockRewards: []
  clientName: Silas
  jobDescription: Finish the direct route from Vance's middle supply point to the
    community. Build a safe 100-meter crossing and observe how its members and supports
    distribute the test vehicle's load.
  budget: 200000
  liveLoadWeight: 1000
  bridgeSpan: 100
  allowedMaterials: []
  hiddenTools: 
  hiddenMaterials:
  - {fileID: 11400000, guid: 4524a3fc876c6b640a735e6808fe1271, type: 2}
  - {fileID: 11400000, guid: 57a46c6632dd61b4094902963cf1c5be, type: 2}
  enforceMaxStress: 0
  maxAllowedStress: 100
  isTimeAttack: 0
  timeAttackDuration: 60
  winCondition: 0
  requiredIntactTime: 5
  goldReward: 500
  expReward: 100
  offerDialogue:
    name: Silas
    sentences:
    - Now that you understand load distribution, let's put that knowledge to use.
    - We need a bridge that connects the community to the main route.
    - The crossing is <b><#E09500>100 meters</color></b> wide.
    - A jeep will test this route before Vance's supplies continue to the community.
    - There's a rock formation partway across, but it sits much lower than the roads
      on either side.
    - <b><#E09500>You'll have to decide how to use the available support points across
      the site</color></b>.
    - Remember, the way you arrange the bridge and its supports affects how the vehicle's
      weight is distributed.
    - <b><#E09500>Watch how the whole structure responds when the jeep crosses</color></b>.
    - If you're ready, take the contract.
  continueOfferDialogue:
    name: Silas
    sentences: []
  reminderDialogue:
    name: Silas
    sentences:
    - Don't rush the design, {PlayerName}.
    - Remember what we discussed about load distribution.
    - Think carefully about where you place the supports, and keep an eye on how
      the whole bridge responds during the test.
  finishedContractDialogue:
    name: Silas
    sentences:
    - The community has a direct connection to the route now. Vance's supplies can
      continue from the middle point.
    - They won't have to take the long way around anymore.
    - That was a wider crossing than your earlier projects.
    - You also got to see how the bridge's design and support arrangement affect
      the way it carries weight.
    - You handled it well, {PlayerName}.
    - I've got a feeling this won't be the last project we handle together.
